{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Orxta","id":"343605682580488215","is_bot":0,"username":"robdor."},"author_id":"343605682580488215","channel_id":"698489628289925130","content":"After some time, an avatar of Solomon walks to the cave. He takes the goggles from where you placed them on their table and simply crushes them in his hand. Sitting in the brittle broken fragments is an ~~infinity stone~~ ioun stone of unknown power. It radiates an intense aura of pure law. \n\n\"Thank you for fulfilling this task. These artifacts have tricky keys to their destruction. Now that you have introduced enough chaos into the world through your lies, the protective spells have failed.\" You can tell that being in the presence of pure law is making the construct of Solomon ill. He directs a team of Uru to pickup the stone and socket it into the crown in the middle of the table. As you look at it. You can see that there are two other stones already in the crown. Only one slot remains to be filled. \"Soon this artifact will have enough power to enact our final plan, and finally bring the world into balance. Again I thank you. Please take this scroll as a reward.\"\n\n(You receive a scroll of Maze  https://www.dndbeyond.com/spells/maze)","created_at":"2020-08-14T02:25:59.839000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"743656641639088280","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
